//RS     // ── Typed route inputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//RS     //
//RS     // Sema binds every handler parameter to one route input: a path
//RS     // parameter by name, the one search record (or a scalar search field),
//RS     // or the route's loader data.  The compiler serializes that binding next
//RS     // to the handler so the runtime decodes each position from the checked
//RS     // navigation, never from a positional guess.
//RS 
